"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkwebsite=globalThis.webpackChunkwebsite||[]).push([[7815],{5971(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2026/01/09/prodcat-vs-markdown","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/prodcat-vs-markdown","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-09-prodcat-vs-markdown.md","title":"Prodcat vs. Manual Markdown: A Time Audit","description":"We ran a time audit comparing a manual Markdown documentation workflow to Prodcat\u2019s automated approach. The results were eye-opening, revealing not just significant time savings but also profound qualitative benefits.","date":"2026-01-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Productivity","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/productivity","description":"Tips and tools to enhance your documentation workflow."},{"inline":false,"label":"Comparison","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/comparison","description":"Blog posts comparing Prodcat with other tools or concepts."},{"inline":false,"label":"Automation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/automation","description":"Explore how Prodcat automates documentation processes."}],"readingTime":2.6,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Prodcat vs. Manual Markdown: A Time Audit","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["productivity","comparison","automation"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"How to Structure Your Product List for Maximum Flexibility","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/structure-product-list"}},"content":"We ran a time audit comparing a manual Markdown documentation workflow to Prodcat\u2019s automated approach. The results were eye-opening, revealing not just significant time savings but also profound qualitative benefits.\\r\\n\\r\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\r\\n\\r\\n## The Experiment: A Head-to-Head Comparison\\r\\n\\r\\nTo quantify the difference, we set up a controlled experiment. The goal was to create a complete documentation site for a catalog of 20 products, each with its own set of features, variants, and specifications.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Team A (Manual Markdown):** This team was tasked with creating the site by hand. This involved writing 20 individual Markdown files for the products, creating and updating category pages, and manually managing all internal linking.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Team B (Prodcat):** This team was given the same product data, but in the form of a single `products.js` file. Their task was to use Prodcat to generate the entire site.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The Quantitative Results: A 90% Time Reduction\\r\\n\\r\\nThe time-tracking data revealed a stark difference in efficiency.\\r\\n\\r\\n| Task | Manual Markdown | Prodcat |\\r\\n| ------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------- |\\r\\n| Initial Product Page Creation | 6 hours | 45 minutes |\\r\\n| Category Linking & Navigation | 2 hours | Automatic (0 min) |\\r\\n| Fixing Broken Links | 1 hour | Automatic (0 min) |\\r\\n| Updating Shared Metadata | 1.5 hours | 10 minutes |\\r\\n| **Total Time** | **10.5 hours** | **~1 hour** |\\r\\n\\r\\nThe result is a **90% reduction** in the time and effort required to launch a complete product documentation site. The time saved is not just a one-off benefit; it compounds with every new product added and every update made.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Beyond the Numbers: The Qualitative Benefits\\r\\n\\r\\nThe audit revealed that the true cost of manual documentation isn\'t just in the hours spent, but also in the quality and consistency of the final product.\\r\\n\\r\\n-   **Guaranteed Consistency:** With Prodcat, every product page is generated from the same template. This ensures a uniform structure, layout, and style across the entire site\u2014a feat that is nearly impossible to achieve manually without rigorous, time-consuming reviews.\\r\\n-   **Effortless Maintenance:** Need to add a new specification to all products? With a manual approach, that\'s 20 files to edit. With Prodcat, it\'s a single change in one template. This drastically reduces the long-term maintenance burden.\\r\\n-   **Built-in SEO and Metadata:** Prodcat automatically generates SEO-friendly URLs and metadata from the product data. This foundational SEO work is often overlooked in manual processes but is critical for discoverability.\\r\\n-   **Faster Contributor Onboarding:** New team members don\'t need to learn a complex file structure or a long list of formatting rules. They only need to learn how to add a product object to a JavaScript file, dramatically lowering the barrier to contribution.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Is Manual Markdown Ever the Right Choice?\\r\\n\\r\\nFor a single, standalone document, Markdown is an excellent tool. But for a collection of structured documents like a product catalog, its limitations become a significant liability. The risk of inconsistency, broken links, and maintenance overhead grows exponentially with each new page.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Conclusion: Upgrade Your Workflow\\r\\n\\r\\nIf you\u2019re still managing a product documentation site by writing Markdown by hand, this audit demonstrates that there is a more efficient, reliable, and scalable way. Prodcat isn\u2019t just faster \u2014 it\u2019s a smarter workflow that delivers a higher-quality result with a fraction of the effort."},{"id":"/2026/01/09/structure-product-list","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/structure-product-list","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-09-structure-product-list.md","title":"How to Structure Your Product List for Maximum Flexibility","description":"Your products.js file is the heart of your Prodcat site. A well-structured product list is essential for creating a documentation site that is clear, scalable, and easy to customize. This guide will walk you through best practices for structuring your products.js file to unlock the full potential of Prodcat.","date":"2026-01-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Tutorial","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/tutorial","description":"Step-by-step guides to help you get the most out of Prodcat."},{"inline":false,"label":"Schema","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/schema","description":"Best practices for structuring your product data."},{"inline":false,"label":"Best Practices","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/best-practices","description":"Recommended strategies and methods for optimal results."}],"readingTime":2.96,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"How to Structure Your Product List for Maximum Flexibility","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["tutorial","schema","best-practices"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Prodcat vs. Manual Markdown: A Time Audit","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/prodcat-vs-markdown"},"nextItem":{"title":"Why We Built Prodcat: From Chaos to Clarity","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/why-we-built-prodcat-from-chaos-to-clarity"}},"content":"Your `products.js` file is the heart of your Prodcat site. A well-structured product list is essential for creating a documentation site that is clear, scalable, and easy to customize. This guide will walk you through best practices for structuring your `products.js` file to unlock the full potential of Prodcat.\\r\\n\\r\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why a Well-Structured `products.js` Matters\\r\\n\\r\\nProdcat reads your product list and generates documentation automatically. The way you structure this list directly impacts the quality and usability of your generated site. A well-designed schema makes your site:\\r\\n\\r\\n-   **Easier to Navigate:** Clear categorization and consistent data allow Prodcat to build intuitive navigation menus and directory pages.\\r\\n-   **More Customizable:** A structured approach makes it simpler to apply custom templates and styling, ensuring your documentation aligns with your brand.\\r\\n-   **Scalable:** As your product line grows, a consistent structure prevents your documentation from becoming a tangled mess.\\r\\n-   **Easier to Maintain:** When all product information is logically organized, updates and additions become straightforward and less error-prone.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Core Product Fields Explained\\r\\n\\r\\nLet\'s break down the recommended structure for a single product entry. Each field serves a specific purpose in generating your documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\n```javascript\\r\\nexport default [\\r\\n  {\\r\\n    id: \\"widget-pro\\",\\r\\n    name: \\"Widget Pro\\",\\r\\n    description: \\"A high-performance widget designed for professional use cases, offering unparalleled speed and reliability.\\",\\r\\n    category: \\"Widgets\\",\\r\\n    price: 199.99,\\r\\n    features: [\\r\\n      \\"Blazing-fast performance\\",\\r\\n      \\"Enterprise-grade reliability\\",\\r\\n      \\"Lightweight and efficient design\\"\\r\\n    ],\\r\\n    variants: [\\r\\n      { name: \\"Standard\\", sku: \\"WP-STD\\" },\\r\\n      { name: \\"Deluxe\\", sku: \\"WP-DLX\\" }\\r\\n    ],\\r\\n  },\\r\\n];\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n-   **`id` (String, Required):** A unique identifier for the product. This is used to generate file names and URLs, so it should be a URL-friendly string (e.g., `widget-pro`, `advanced-gadget-v2`).\\r\\n-   **`name` (String, Required):** The official name of the product. This will be used as the main heading on the product page.\\r\\n-   **`description` (String, Required):** A detailed description of the product. This is your opportunity to provide a comprehensive overview. You can use Markdown here for formatting.\\r\\n-   **`category` (String):** The primary category the product belongs to. Prodcat uses this to group products and create category-specific pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Leveraging Categories for Better Navigation\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `category` field is fundamental to organizing your site. By assigning categories consistently, you enable users to easily browse related products. For example, a `products.js` file with multiple products might look like this:\\r\\n\\r\\n```javascript\\r\\nexport default [\\r\\n  { id: \\"widget-pro\\", name: \\"Widget Pro\\", category: \\"Widgets\\", ... },\\r\\n  { id: \\"widget-basic\\", name: \\"Widget Basic\\", category: \\"Widgets\\", ... },\\r\\n  { id: \\"gadget-plus\\", name: \\"Gadget Plus\\", category: \\"Gadgets\\", ... },\\r\\n];\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nProdcat will automatically generate a \\"Widgets\\" page listing both \\"Widget Pro\\" and \\"Widget Basic,\\" and a separate \\"Gadgets\\" page for \\"Gadget Plus.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n## Using Features to Highlight Key Selling Points\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `features` array is perfect for showcasing the key benefits of your product. Each string in the array will be rendered as a list item, making it easy for customers to scan.\\r\\n\\r\\n```javascript\\r\\nfeatures: [\\r\\n  \\"Feature A: Solves a common problem\\",\\r\\n  \\"Feature B: Improves efficiency\\",\\r\\n  \\"Feature C: Integrates with other tools\\"\\r\\n],\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nUse this section to be concise and impactful.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Managing Product Variants Effectively\\r\\n\\r\\nFor products that come in different versions (e.g., sizes, colors, or feature tiers), the `variants` array is indispensable. Each object in the array represents a unique variant.\\r\\n\\r\\n```javascript\\r\\nvariants: [\\r\\n  { name: \\"Standard\\", sku: \\"WP-STD\\", price: 199.99 },\\r\\n  { name: \\"Deluxe\\", sku: \\"WP-DLX\\", price: 299.99, features: [\\"Additional premium feature\\"] }\\r\\n],\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can even include a `price` or additional `features` within a variant object to override the main product\'s properties. This provides a high degree of flexibility.\\r\\n\\r\\nBy following these structuring guidelines, you can ensure that your `products.js` file is a robust foundation for a high-quality, maintainable, and scalable product documentation site."},{"id":"/2026/01/09/why-we-built-prodcat-from-chaos-to-clarity","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/why-we-built-prodcat-from-chaos-to-clarity","source":"@site/blog/2026-01-09-why-we-built-prodcat-from-chaos-to-clarity.md","title":"Why We Built Prodcat: From Chaos to Clarity","description":"Maintaining product documentation was eating our time and sanity. We built Prodcat to fix that \u2014 and here\u2019s how it changed everything. It\u2019s the story of moving from a state of constant, low-grade chaos to one of structure and clarity.","date":"2026-01-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Prodcat","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/prodcat","description":"Articles related to the Prodcat tool and its features."},{"inline":false,"label":"Origin Story","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/origin-story","description":"The story behind why Prodcat was created."},{"inline":false,"label":"Documentation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/documentation","description":"Articles about creating and managing software product documentation."}],"readingTime":2.84,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Why We Built Prodcat: From Chaos to Clarity","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["prodcat","origin-story","documentation"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"How to Structure Your Product List for Maximum Flexibility","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/structure-product-list"},"nextItem":{"title":"Getting Started with Prodcat: A Beginner\'s Guide","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/31/getting-started-with-prodcat"}},"content":"Maintaining product documentation was eating our time and sanity. We built Prodcat to fix that \u2014 and here\u2019s how it changed everything. It\u2019s the story of moving from a state of constant, low-grade chaos to one of structure and clarity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\r\\n\\r\\n## The Breaking Point: A Cascade of Small Problems\\r\\n\\r\\nBefore Prodcat, our documentation process was a fragile system held together by manual effort and wishful thinking. We were juggling dozens of Markdown files across multiple product lines. The workflow was not just inefficient; it was a constant source of errors.\\r\\n\\r\\n-   **Inconsistent Information:** A price update meant hunting down every instance of that price across multiple files. A changed feature name could linger in old documents for months.\\r\\n-   **Broken Navigation:** Every new product required manually adding links to category pages and navigation bars. It was tedious and incredibly easy to miss a link or create a broken one.\\r\\n-   **Onboarding Nightmare:** Bringing a new team member up to speed was a challenge. There was no single source of truth, just a collection of files with their own quirks and histories.\\r\\n-   **Slow to Scale:** Launching a new product or a new product line was a monumental task that involved more copy-pasting than innovation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe collective weight of these \\"small\\" problems was immense. It was death by a thousand paper cuts.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The \'Aha!\' Moment: Documentation as Data\\r\\n\\r\\nThe turning point came when we stopped thinking about our documentation as a collection of static pages and started thinking about it as data. Our products had names, descriptions, prices, and features. This was structured information, so why were we managing it in an unstructured way?\\r\\n\\r\\nWe asked ourselves: _What if our documentation could be generated from a single, canonical source of truth?_\\r\\n\\r\\nThis simple question was the genesis of Prodcat. We envisioned a tool that would take a simple JavaScript array of product objects and handle the rest. No more Markdown files to wrangle. No more broken links to fix. Just clean, consistent, and automatically generated documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Our Core Principles in Building Prodcat\\r\\n\\r\\nThat vision evolved into a philosophy that guided Prodcat\'s development. We built it around three core principles:\\r\\n\\r\\n1.  **Centralize Your Data:** There should only be one place to update product information. The `products.js` file became our single source of truth. Change a product\'s name there, and it changes everywhere on the site.\\r\\n2.  **Automate the Boring Parts:** Manual, repetitive tasks are a recipe for errors and burnout. Prodcat was designed to automate the entire process of creating product pages, directory pages, and navigation.\\r\\n3.  **Focus on What Matters \u2014 Your Products:** Developers and product managers should spend their time building and improving products, not wrestling with documentation tools. Prodcat frees them to do just that.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The Transformation: From Chaos to Clarity\\r\\n\\r\\nImplementing Prodcat internally was transformative. The chaos of managing dozens of individual files was replaced by the clarity of a single, well-structured data source.\\r\\n\\r\\n-   **Updates became trivial.** A feature change now requires editing a single line in one file.\\r\\n-   **Consistency is now guaranteed.** Every product page follows the same template, ensuring a uniform and professional user experience.\\r\\n-   **Scaling is now effortless.** Adding a new product is as simple as adding a new object to an array.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you\u2019re documenting hardware, software, or services, Prodcat is designed to help you scale your documentation without sacrificing clarity or your team\'s sanity. It\'s the tool we wish we\'d had from the start."},{"id":"/2025/12/31/getting-started-with-prodcat","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/31/getting-started-with-prodcat","source":"@site/blog/2025-12-31-getting-started-with-prodcat.md","title":"Getting Started with Prodcat: A Beginner\'s Guide","description":"Welcome to the Prodcat blog! In this article, we\'ll walk you through the basics of getting started with Prodcat. Whether you\'re a small business owner, a developer, or just someone who wants to create a beautiful product documentation website, Prodcat is the tool for you.","date":"2025-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Prodcat","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/prodcat","description":"Articles related to the Prodcat tool and its features."},{"inline":false,"label":"Getting Started","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/getting-started","description":"Introductory guides to using Prodcat."},{"inline":false,"label":"Documentation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/documentation","description":"Articles about creating and managing software product documentation."}],"readingTime":1.84,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Getting Started with Prodcat: A Beginner\'s Guide","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["prodcat","getting-started","documentation"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Why We Built Prodcat: From Chaos to Clarity","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2026/01/09/why-we-built-prodcat-from-chaos-to-clarity"},"nextItem":{"title":"Why Your Business Needs a Product Documentation Website","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/30/why-your-business-needs-a-product-documentation-website"}},"content":"Welcome to the Prodcat blog! In this article, we\'ll walk you through the basics of getting started with Prodcat. Whether you\'re a small business owner, a developer, or just someone who wants to create a beautiful product documentation website, Prodcat is the tool for you.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What is Prodcat?\\n\\nProdcat is a powerful tool that allows you to generate a professional product documentation website from a simple list of products. With Prodcat, you can create a beautiful, feature-rich website in minutes, without any prior experience in web development.\\n\\n## Step 1: Installation\\n\\nThe first step is to install Prodcat. You can do this by running the following command in your terminal:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install -g prodcat\\n```\\n\\nThis will install Prodcat globally on your system, so you can use it from anywhere.\\n\\n## Step 2: Initialization\\n\\nOnce you have Prodcat installed, you can create a new project by running the `prodcat init` command. This will create a new directory with the basic project structure.\\n\\n```bash\\nprodcat init my-product-site\\n```\\n\\nThis will create a new directory called `my-product-site` with all the necessary files to get started.\\n\\n## Step 3: Add Your Products\\n\\nThe next step is to add your products to the `products.js` file. This file is located in the root of your project directory, and it\'s where you\'ll define all of your products. Here\'s an example of what a product object looks like:\\n\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  id: \'prod1\',\\n  name: \'Sample Product\',\\n  description: \'This is a sample product.\',\\n  price: \'$99.99\',\\n  features: [\'Feature 1\', \'Feature 2\'],\\n  specifications: [\\n    { key: \'Weight\', value: \'1kg\' },\\n    { key: \'Dimensions\', value: \'10x10x10 cm\' }\\n  ],\\n  images: [\'/img/prod1.jpg\']\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Step 4: Generate Your Website\\n\\nOnce you\'ve added your products, you can generate your website by running the `prodcat generate` command.\\n\\n```bash\\nprodcat generate\\n```\\n\\nThis will generate a static HTML website in the `website/build` directory.\\n\\n## Step 5: View Your Website\\n\\nThat\'s it! You can now view your website by opening the `website/build/index.html` file in your browser. Or, you can run `npm start` in the `website` directory to start a local development server.\\n\\nWe hope this guide has been helpful. If you have any questions, feel free to reach out to us on [GitHub](https://github.com/your-repo/prodcat)."},{"id":"/2025/12/30/why-your-business-needs-a-product-documentation-website","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/30/why-your-business-needs-a-product-documentation-website","source":"@site/blog/2025-12-30-why-your-business-needs-a-product-documentation-website.md","title":"Why Your Business Needs a Product Documentation Website","description":"In today\'s digital age, having an online presence is crucial for any business. But what about a product documentation website? Is it really necessary? In this article, we\'ll explore why your business needs a product documentation website and how it can benefit you.","date":"2025-12-30T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Prodcat","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/prodcat","description":"Articles related to the Prodcat tool and its features."},{"inline":false,"label":"Business","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/business","description":"Articles discussing the business benefits of product documentation."},{"inline":false,"label":"Documentation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/documentation","description":"Articles about creating and managing software product documentation."},{"inline":false,"label":"Marketing","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/marketing","description":"How product documentation can assist in marketing efforts."}],"readingTime":1.7,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Why Your Business Needs a Product Documentation Website","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["prodcat","business","documentation","marketing"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Getting Started with Prodcat: A Beginner\'s Guide","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/31/getting-started-with-prodcat"},"nextItem":{"title":"The Power of Automation: How Prodcat Saves You Time","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/29/the-power-of-automation-how-prodcat-saves-you-time"}},"content":"In today\'s digital age, having an online presence is crucial for any business. But what about a product documentation website? Is it really necessary? In this article, we\'ll explore why your business needs a product documentation website and how it can benefit you.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## 1. Improved Customer Experience\\n\\nA well-structured product documentation website can significantly improve the customer experience. It provides your customers with a single source of truth for all your products, making it easy for them to find the information they need. This can lead to increased customer satisfaction and loyalty.\\n\\n## 2. Reduced Support Costs\\n\\nA comprehensive product documentation website can also help you reduce support costs. By providing your customers with the information they need to solve their own problems, you can reduce the number of support tickets and phone calls your team has to handle. This can free up your support team to focus on more complex issues.\\n\\n## 3. Increased Sales\\n\\nA product documentation website can also help you increase sales. By providing potential customers with detailed information about your products, you can help them make an informed purchasing decision. This can lead to increased conversion rates and more sales for your business.\\n\\n## 4. Improved SEO\\n\\nA product documentation website can also help you improve your search engine optimization (SEO). By creating high-quality, keyword-rich content, you can attract more organic traffic to your website. This can lead to increased brand awareness and more potential customers.\\n\\n## 5. A Professional Image\\n\\nFinally, a product documentation website can help you project a professional image to your customers. A well-designed, easy-to-use website shows that you\'re a serious business that cares about its customers. This can help you build trust and credibility with your audience.\\n\\nIn conclusion, a product documentation website is a valuable asset for any business. It can help you improve the customer experience, reduce support costs, increase sales, improve your SEO, and project a professional image. And with a tool like Prodcat, creating a product documentation website has never been easier."},{"id":"/2025/12/29/the-power-of-automation-how-prodcat-saves-you-time","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/29/the-power-of-automation-how-prodcat-saves-you-time","source":"@site/blog/2025-12-29-the-power-of-automation-how-prodcat-saves-you-time.md","title":"The Power of Automation: How Prodcat Saves You Time","description":"In today\'s fast-paced world, time is a precious commodity. That\'s why automation is so important. In this article, we\'ll explore how Prodcat uses automation to save you time and effort when creating a product documentation website.","date":"2025-12-29T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Prodcat","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/prodcat","description":"Articles related to the Prodcat tool and its features."},{"inline":false,"label":"Automation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/automation","description":"Explore how Prodcat automates documentation processes."},{"inline":false,"label":"Time-saving","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/time-saving","description":"Tips and features in Prodcat that help save time."}],"readingTime":1.79,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"The Power of Automation: How Prodcat Saves You Time","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["prodcat","automation","time-saving"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Why Your Business Needs a Product Documentation Website","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/30/why-your-business-needs-a-product-documentation-website"},"nextItem":{"title":"Customizing Your Prodcat Website: A Deep Dive","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/28/customizing-your-prodcat-website-a-deep-dive"}},"content":"In today\'s fast-paced world, time is a precious commodity. That\'s why automation is so important. In this article, we\'ll explore how Prodcat uses automation to save you time and effort when creating a product documentation website.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Manual vs. Automated\\n\\nTraditionally, creating a website has been a manual and time-consuming process. You had to write the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, and then you had to manually create a page for each of your products. This could take days, or even weeks, depending on the number of products you have.\\n\\nWith Prodcat, the entire process is automated. You simply add your products to a `products.js` file, and Prodcat does the rest. It automatically generates a page for each of your products, as well as a main landing page and a categories page.\\n\\n## How it Works\\n\\nProdcat uses a combination of technologies to automate the process of creating a website. It uses Node.js to read your `products.js` file, and then it uses Handlebars to generate Markdown files for each of your products. Finally, it uses Docusaurus to generate a static HTML website from the Markdown files.\\n\\nThe entire process is seamless and transparent. You don\'t need to know anything about Node.js, Handlebars, or Docusaurus to use Prodcat. You just need to know how to add your products to the `products.js` file.\\n\\n## The Benefits of Automation\\n\\nThe benefits of automation are clear. By automating the process of creating a website, Prodcat can save you a significant amount of time and effort. This allows you to focus on what you do best: creating great products.\\n\\nBut the benefits of automation go beyond time savings. By automating the process, Prodcat also ensures that your website is consistent and professional. You don\'t have to worry about making a mistake or forgetting to update a page. Prodcat takes care of all the details for you.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nIn conclusion, Prodcat is a powerful tool that uses automation to save you time and effort when creating a product documentation website. It\'s the perfect solution for businesses and individuals who want to create a professional-looking website without spending a lot of time and money."},{"id":"/2025/12/28/customizing-your-prodcat-website-a-deep-dive","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/28/customizing-your-prodcat-website-a-deep-dive","source":"@site/blog/2025-12-28-customizing-your-prodcat-website-a-deep-dive.md","title":"Customizing Your Prodcat Website: A Deep Dive","description":"One of the great things about Prodcat is that it\'s highly customizable. In this article, we\'ll take a deep dive into the different ways you can customize your Prodcat website to match your brand and meet your needs.","date":"2025-12-28T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Prodcat","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/prodcat","description":"Articles related to the Prodcat tool and its features."},{"inline":false,"label":"Customization","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/customization","description":"Guides on how to customize your Prodcat website."},{"inline":false,"label":"Theming","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/theming","description":"Articles about changing the visual theme of your Prodcat site."},{"inline":false,"label":"Templates","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/templates","description":"How-to guides for using and creating custom Handlebars templates in Prodcat."}],"readingTime":1.83,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Customizing Your Prodcat Website: A Deep Dive","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["prodcat","customization","theming","templates"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"The Power of Automation: How Prodcat Saves You Time","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/29/the-power-of-automation-how-prodcat-saves-you-time"},"nextItem":{"title":"Prodcat vs. The World: Why Prodcat is the Best Choice for Product Documentation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/27/prodcat-vs-the-world"}},"content":"One of the great things about Prodcat is that it\'s highly customizable. In this article, we\'ll take a deep dive into the different ways you can customize your Prodcat website to match your brand and meet your needs.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Theming\\n\\nThe easiest way to customize your Prodcat website is by modifying the CSS. Prodcat uses the Infima CSS framework, which is highly customizable. You can change the color palette, typography, and other aspects of the design by modifying the `website/src/css/custom.css` file.\\n\\nYou can also customize the Docusaurus components by \\"swizzling\\" them. Swizzling allows you to replace a theme component with your own implementation. This is a powerful feature that gives you full control over the markup and logic of the components.\\n\\n## Templates\\n\\nProdcat uses Handlebars to generate the Markdown files for your product pages and directories. The templates are located in the `templates` directory of your Prodcat project. You can modify these templates to change the structure and content of the generated Markdown files.\\n\\nFor example, you could add new sections to the product pages or change the layout of the product directory. The templates are written in Handlebars, which is a simple and powerful templating language.\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\nProdcat has two main configuration files: `prodcat.config.js` and `website/docusaurus.config.js`. These files allow you to customize various aspects of your website, such as the site\'s title, logo, navbar, and footer.\\n\\nYou can also use these files to configure more advanced features, such as search integration and internationalization.\\n\\n## Plugins\\n\\nFinally, you can extend the functionality of Prodcat by creating your own plugins. The plugin system allows you to add new commands to the CLI, modify the build process, or integrate with other tools and services.\\n\\nThis is an advanced feature that requires some knowledge of Node.js and the Prodcat codebase. But it\'s a powerful way to extend the functionality of Prodcat and tailor it to your specific needs.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nIn conclusion, Prodcat is a highly customizable tool that allows you to create a product documentation website that\'s a perfect fit for your brand. Whether you\'re a beginner or an experienced developer, you\'ll find plenty of ways to customize your Prodcat website and make it your own."},{"id":"/2025/12/27/prodcat-vs-the-world","metadata":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/27/prodcat-vs-the-world","source":"@site/blog/2025-12-27-prodcat-vs-the-world.md","title":"Prodcat vs. The World: Why Prodcat is the Best Choice for Product Documentation","description":"There are a lot of tools out there for creating documentation websites. So why should you choose Prodcat? In this article, we\'ll compare Prodcat to some of the other popular options and explain why we think Prodcat is the best choice for product documentation.","date":"2025-12-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Prodcat","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/prodcat","description":"Articles related to the Prodcat tool and its features."},{"inline":false,"label":"Comparison","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/comparison","description":"Blog posts comparing Prodcat with other tools or concepts."},{"inline":false,"label":"Documentation","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/tags/documentation","description":"Articles about creating and managing software product documentation."}],"readingTime":1.74,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ion Gireada","title":"Node.js CLI & AI Solutions Developer | Championing Pristine Software Documentation","url":"https://github.com/ioncakephper","page":{"permalink":"/prodcat/blog/authors/ioncakephper"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ion-gireada-223929/","github":"https://github.com/ioncakephper"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/ioncakephper.png","key":"ioncakephper"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Prodcat vs. The World: Why Prodcat is the Best Choice for Product Documentation","authors":"ioncakephper","tags":["prodcat","comparison","documentation"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Customizing Your Prodcat Website: A Deep Dive","permalink":"/prodcat/blog/2025/12/28/customizing-your-prodcat-website-a-deep-dive"}},"content":"There are a lot of tools out there for creating documentation websites. So why should you choose Prodcat? In this article, we\'ll compare Prodcat to some of the other popular options and explain why we think Prodcat is the best choice for product documentation.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Prodcat vs. WordPress\\n\\nWordPress is a popular choice for creating websites, but it\'s not the best choice for product documentation. WordPress is a general-purpose CMS, which means it\'s not optimized for documentation. It can be difficult to create a well-structured documentation website with WordPress, and it can be even more difficult to maintain it over time.\\n\\nProdcat, on the other hand, is specifically designed for product documentation. It\'s easy to create a well-structured website with Prodcat, and it\'s even easier to maintain it.\\n\\n## Prodcat vs. Read the Docs\\n\\nRead the Docs is a popular platform for hosting documentation, but it\'s not a documentation generator. You still have to write the documentation yourself, and then you have to upload it to Read the Docs.\\n\\nWith Prodcat, the entire process is automated. You simply add your products to a `products.js` file, and Prodcat does the rest. It automatically generates a beautiful, feature-rich website for you.\\n\\n## Prodcat vs. Docusaurus\\n\\nProdcat is built on top of Docusaurus, which is a popular static site generator. But Docusaurus is a general-purpose tool, which means it\'s not optimized for product documentation. You still have to do a lot of work to create a product documentation website with Docusaurus.\\n\\nProdcat takes care of all the heavy lifting for you. It provides you with a pre-configured Docusaurus project that\'s optimized for product documentation. It also provides you with a set of Handlebars templates that you can use to generate your product pages.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nIn conclusion, there are a lot of tools out there for creating documentation websites. But if you\'re looking for a tool that\'s specifically designed for product documentation, then Prodcat is the best choice for you. It\'s easy to use, it\'s highly customizable, and it\'s built on top of the best technologies available."}]}}')}}]);